    <title>On a Family of Twisted Trace Curves over Finite Fields, and Fibonacci Numbers</title>
    <updated>2021-02-03T14:33:06Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2102.02081v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2102.02081v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>We present some results about the number of rational points on a certain family of curves defined over a finite field. In a small number of cases the curves have more rational points than expected. Fibonacci numbers make an appearance, as do cyclotomic polynomials.</summary>
